      "math_academy_id": "q-35685",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C$ given that\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
